# TASK-005 — Core Module Architecture & Dependencies
## BATCH-002 — Business Core Architecture Knowledge Collection

**Application:** Teranoo ERP Knowledge Hub

**Previous task:** TASK-004 — Independently approved with targeted notes.

**Development mode:** Incremental implementation under independent supervision.

---

## 1. Mission

Implement the second substantial official knowledge collection, dedicated to the architecture of the four core business modules of Teranoo ERP.

The objective is to teach readers how to architect a modular enterprise ERP product, establish module boundaries, assign data ownership, classify dependencies, coordinate integrations, and preserve independent module activation.

The application must explain not only what Teranoo ERP has decided, but also what those decisions mean, why they matter, how they relate to one another, and how they will influence future functional design and implementation.

Preserve all approved functionality from TASK-001 through TASK-004.

Do not rebuild the application or redesign its global visual identity.

Do not start TASK-006.

